        5,
        10
      ],
      "type": "translation_and_reading_condition",
      "current": "Cues are needed during extended rests where useful, not merely after them; retain tempo and meter changes. Next entry, rather than next measure, confirms the doubled instrument."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        8
      ],
      "type": "translation_and_reading_condition",
      "current": "Accordion binding is an exception for rare page-turn situations, not a permission based on low page count; roughly40sides and paper weight condition coil-binding advice."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        4,
        5,
        10
      ],
      "type": "judgment",
      "current": "System-start measure position, multirest duration/range, rehearsal landmark and audible cue serve separate tasks. Film/Music Theatre retain individual measure numbering as an explicit exception."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "type": "judgment",
      "current": "A cover may provide instructions or change the music opening to page2 for a turn. Recheck physical spreads. Staff height is bottom-to-top, not one space; orchestra/solo scope remains separate."
    },
    {
      "pdf_pages": [
        8,
        12
      ],
      "type": "judgment",
      "current": "Proofread both horizontal musical continuity and vertical relationships. Anchored objects and preserved playback do not establish readable placement after a layout change."
